        "Slowly round the back and bring the torso toward the legs only through a controllable range. Gentle abdominal activity can accompany the movement; maximal bracing is not required. Avoid forcing the shoulders or neck downward, breathe easily and hold. Then ease the grip as needed and slowly return to a more upright sitting position."
