        "Do not force greater rounding or chest-to-thigh contact. If pain, tingling or sharp pressure occurs, reduce the range and leave the position. Do not force the knees straight. Slight knee bending can reduce the pull at the backs of the legs; note it as a modification. This position deliberately rounds the spine and is distinct from a straight-backed hip hinge."
